                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">This course consists of 12 hours of theoretical study, 35 hours of social practice and 3 hours of reflection reports. The content of social practice varies from base to base, mainly including: under the guidance of rehabilitation therapists, participating in rehabilitation training activities such as motor coordination, hand-eye fine motor skills, and visual-spatial skills for special children; or communicate and interact with the elderly, and provide the necessary specialized care services; or learn to provide rehabilitation nursing services for patients with chronic diseases such as neuromyopathy; or participate in postpartum home visits, learn about community population immunization programs, etc.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
